      {
        "id": 177890,
        "name": "The Burning Stickman",
        "username": "The_Burning_Stickman",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_burning_stickman/{size}/2003_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-06-20T15:23:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Powerhound_2000\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/powerhound_2000/48/1859_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Powerhound_2000:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>That makes for a long game especially if you ended up at five heroes if you play it out. &nbsp; Though thinking about it setting up a team which shuts down the villain deck every round is going to make for a long game as it means your damage output it likely low. &nbsp;</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Not necessarily – I ended up with all of Omnitron-X's damaging Components out while I was waiting for Take Down and Mental Divergence to be drawn (somehow, whenever I want to test a set-up like this, the cards I need for it end up in the bottom half of the deck), and Visionary can get Demoralization out.</p>\n<p>(I actually ended up Self-Sabotaging the damaging components away because it was starting to look like Voss was going to get taken out before I managed to get the set-up going.)</p>\n<p>If Legacy gets his ring out (or you're using Young Legacy), he can also maintain a damage presence pretty reliably – and, since you've got the villain deck locked down, minions are a non-issue.</p>\n<p>While the set-up depends on Legacy, it can be any Legacy (so Young Legacy can start and keep blasting, for instance) and it won't interrupt or stall his play-power-draw, and the other two can be whoever you want. With the villain deck locked down, you could easily round out the team with pure damage dealers like Ra or Haka.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:01:57.719Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
